**Day 31: Introduction to NoSQL**  

**Topic:**  
Introduction to NoSQL databases, exploring why NoSQL exists, its types (document, key-value, column-family, graph), and its practical use cases compared to traditional relational databases.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand the need for NoSQL in modern applications.  
• Differentiate between RDBMS and NoSQL databases.  
• Identify real-world scenarios where NoSQL is preferred.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Draw a comparison chart: RDBMS vs 4 NoSQL types.  
• Discuss real-world examples of NoSQL implementations.  
• Research and present use cases for each NoSQL type.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• NoSQL types: document, key-value, column-family, graph.  
• Scalability and flexibility of NoSQL databases.  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• N/A (Focus on NoSQL concepts).  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Document stores (e.g., MongoDB) for dynamic schema applications.  
• Key-value stores (e.g., Redis) for caching and session management.  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• Draw.io (for creating visual comparisons).  
• Research materials and case studies.  

**Summary:**  
Explored the fundamentals of NoSQL, its types, and its advantages over traditional RDBMS. Created a comparative chart and discussed practical applications, emphasizing scalability and flexibility in modern data management.  

